/*
 * TModule.h.ct - the TIR object model (S1b-S1, docs/design/tir-lir-contract.md §1-§3).
 *
 * TIR is a typed shadow of the AST: it records the facts the emitter derives
 * while it prints (type ids, value classes, resolved call targets, ownership
 * actions, scopes and cleanup entries) so a later stage can lower from a typed
 * tree instead of re-reading the AST. This unit owns the object model and
 * every table; it reads no source and emits nothing. S1 only builds the
 * shadow and verifies it -- the AST -> C path stays the only writer.
 *
 * All cross-object references are `int` ids, `0` means "none" and an id is
 * never reused. Arrays append in source order. The pool is process scoped
 * (build mode appends one slice per unit, compile mode has one unit) and is
 * released with the process. Counting tables double up to `CAP_LIMIT`, the
 * S1a-0 capacity rule.
 *
 * The enum vocabularies are `#define`s, not `pub enum`: this codebase spells
 * node vocabularies as integer macros (Arena.h.ct kinds, Emitter's N_*
 * mirrors) and a macro does not cross a unit. TBuilder.h.ct repeats the values
 * it needs; `test/ir/run.sh` compares the two blocks number by number.
 *
 * TGraph is a skeleton here (nodes, edges, add + dedupe); S1b-S3 moves it to
 * `backend/tir/TGraph.h.ct` and adds liveness and cycle analysis.
 *
 * `free_param` exists because a generic template body still names `T`: such a
 * type may only be used inside a template, and `used_concrete` records the
 * first use outside one (verifier V1).
 *
 * License: same as the rest of the compiler (see LICENSE / LICENSE.EXCEPTION).
 */
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <time.h>
import runtime::text::Intern;
import frontend::type::TypeCheck;

/* cap mirrors: frontend/sym/Limits.h.ct is authoritative; tools/limits_sync.py checks them. */
#define CAP_LIMIT 65536
#define NODE_LIMIT 16777216

namespace backend::tir;

